--- body ---
## Context

Ticket 1370 (PR #2048) scrubs the seat stderr excerpt in `scripts/gaze_seat.py`
(`SCRUB_PATTERNS`, `scrub`, `stderr_excerpt`) before it reaches the permanent,
pushed `refs/notes/review`. Gaze on its last head (cross-family seat
openai/gpt-6.1-sol, plus the orchestrator's probes) reproduced shapes that
still pass, all non-blocking for 1370's named classes:

- backslash-escaped JSON keys from nested error messages: `{\"access_token\": \"...\"}`;
- a label with a space: `Account ID: <uuid>`;
- over-redaction: the case-insensitive `Basic` pattern eats the word after
  ordinary prose ("basic usage: run"), and in compact JSON a secret field
  swallows every later field up to the next space.

Boundary left by 1370: the seat report body and the codex `-o` outfile are
not scrubbed. A seat's read-only sandbox can read host files; whether gaze
answers quote seat bodies verbatim into notes was not checked.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The three leak/over-redaction shapes above have a test each, red before the fix (author ruling 2026-10-30: the two leak shapes are fixed in ticket 1378; the over-redaction shapes, `basic usage` and compact JSON, are won't-fix: over-redaction is the friction-free failure)
- [ ] It is established, with a positive control, whether seat report text reaches `refs/notes/review` verbatim; if it does, that path is scrubbed the same way, otherwise the boundary is stated in `skills/gaze/references/panel.md`

## Plan (raid 80974c: Imagine, Blind-Spot, feasibility)

Premise holds: all three shapes reproduce on `scrub()` at origin/main 5a8da15a.
Seat bodies reach `refs/notes/review` when the gaze orchestrator quotes them
into its result file (`panel.md` § dissent kept verbatim → `gaze_close.py`
reads `--comment-file` and adds it as the `answer` entry). That counts as
"reaches verbatim", so the second criterion takes its scrub branch.

Actions:
1. Red tests first in `tests/test_gaze_seat.py` (parametrized scrub cases): escaped
   JSON key, `Account ID: <uuid>`, `basic usage: run` survives, compact JSON
   `{"api_key":"…","model":"x","status":500}` keeps `model` and `status`.
   Keep the `session id: <uuid>` survival case.
2. `SCRUB_PATTERNS`: allow `\\` before the key quote; `account[\s_-]?id`;
   value ends at its closing quote or at `,}` / whitespace; `Basic` only before
   a base64-shaped token, case-sensitive.
3. Positive control: plant a canary secret in a seat report, quote it into a
   result file as gaze does, close, grep the note; show it present before the
   fix and redacted after.
4. Scrub the answer text in `gaze_close.py` before it is added, importing
   `gaze_seat.scrub` (no copied patterns).
5. Blind-Spot guard: scrubbing a real answer leaves the verdict,
   `reviewed_head_sha` and `seat:` lines byte-identical; the
   `/home/<login>` rule must not break parsed fields (scope the scrub to free
   text if needed). State the boundary in `skills/gaze/references/panel.md`.

Feasibility: PASS (paths and lines checked: gaze_seat.py:478-495,
gaze_close.py:352). Shares `tests/test_gaze_seat.py` with 1376: appended
tests only, second lander rebases.
